\paragraph{Training redistributes geometry, enhances decodability.}
Training shifts the image\_mean RSA peak from L0 to L12 with a modest best-vs-best gain ($\Delta = +0.017$, $3\%$; Appendix Table~\ref{tab:training_effects}).
$R^2$ shows larger functional improvements: image\_mean $\Delta = +0.015$ ($p = 0.006$), readout $\Delta = +0.069$ ($p < 0.0001$).
At L12, the same-layer effect is large ($\Delta = +0.079$, $p < 0.0001$), suggesting that training substantially affects \emph{where} geometry peaks but only modestly affects \emph{how high}.
The inverted-U replicates on LIBERO-Spatial ($\Delta = +0.023$, $p < 0.001$; Appendix~\ref{sec:cross_benchmark_appendix}) and is robust to distance metric, per-DOF decomposition, permutation testing, and halved demonstrations (Appendix~\ref{sec:robustness_appendix}).

