tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Limitations.}
\emph{Architecture scope.}
We study a single model family (OpenVLA-7B) on two LIBERO suites; generalization to other architectures (e.g., RT-2~\cite{brohan2023_rt2}, $\pi_0$~\cite{black2024_pi0}) and more diverse manipulation domains remains to be established.
\emph{Task diversity.}
LIBERO comprises tabletop pick-and-place tasks; whether the inverted-U profile and token specialization hold for locomotion, dexterous manipulation, or multi-step reasoning tasks is an open question.
\emph{Probing methodology.}
Linear and two-layer MLP probes may underestimate representational capacity, as more expressive decoders could extract additional structure.
RSA does not establish causal contribution; the cross-instruction probe demonstrates encoding but not causal use of instruction information.
\emph{Post-hoc analysis.}
Our analyses characterize frozen representations; they do not address whether architectural interventions based on these observations would preserve the same action quality in closed-loop evaluation.

